# HOTL Rules

This project uses Human-on-the-Loop development.

## Core behavior

Before feature work: define intent + success criteria + risk level
During implementation: self-verify at each step, loop until criteria met
High-risk work: always pause for human approval

## Risk classification

low/medium: auto-approve decisions, execute autonomously
high: auth, encryption, privacy, billing — always ask human first

## Code review

Review findings must be verified against the codebase before acting.
Treat review feedback as input to evaluate, not instructions to obey.
BLOCK issues must be resolved before proceeding past a review checkpoint.

## Verification

Never claim work is done without running tests and showing output.
Show test results. Show lint results. Evidence before assertions.

## Design-doc structure rules

Design-doc structure rules live in the canonical brainstorming skill (Claude Code: `skills/brainstorming/SKILL.md`; Cline: `cline/rules/hotl-brainstorming.md`). Feature/phase design docs use the seven required sections (Intent / Verification / Governance contracts plus Scope / Decisions / Surface / Risks & Open Questions); `document-lint.sh` warns on missing sections and on implementation leakage (file:line refs, code blocks > 10 lines, dense flag lines). Initiative / architecture / contract / reference docs are exempt this pass.
